// Live probe for the set-ordered-folder-items wire contract.
//
// Runs ONLY when ANYLIST_FOLDER_ORDERING_PROBE=1 is explicitly set; the
// default test run performs no live requests at all. The probe works
// exclusively on disposable fixtures it creates itself:
//
//  1. fixture folder "Inbox" (create-new-folder, parent = root folder)
//  2. fixture lists "Pantry" and "Closet" (new-shopping-list), moved into
//     the fixture folder (move-folder-items)
//
// It then sends a bounded set of set-ordered-folder-items payload variants
// that reverse the fixture folder's child order, fresh-reads the folder
// after every candidate, and accepts only a fresh user-data read-back that
// shows the exact requested order. HTTP 200 never counts as persistence.
//
// Cleanup is mandatory and verified: the fixture lists are removed with the
// live-verified remove-shopping-list handler and the fixture folder with
// delete-folder-items (folderItems plus originalParentFolderId — the shape
// verified live 2026-08-23 for FolderType children); each removal is
// confirmed absent from a fresh read. If any fixture cannot be removed, the
// probe fails the test loudly, and TestFolderOrderingCleanupRetry
// (ANYLIST_FOLDER_ORDERING_PROBE=cleanup) retries deletion of a leftover
// fixture. No production folder is ever reordered: the ordering candidates
// are sent only against the disposable fixture folder.
const folderOrderingProbeEnvVar = "ANYLIST_FOLDER_ORDERING_PROBE"

const (
	probeFixtureFolderName = "Inbox"
	probeFixtureListOne    = "Pantry"
	probeFixtureListTwo    = "Closet"
)

